---
import "@fontsource-variable/fraunces/wght.css";
import "@fontsource/atkinson-hyperlegible-next/latin-400.css";
import "@fontsource/atkinson-hyperlegible-next/latin-600.css";
import "../styles/home.css";
import RoomIllustration from "../components/home/RoomIllustration.astro";
import HomeChoices from "../components/home/HomeChoices.astro";
import HomePeople from "../components/home/HomePeople.astro";
import { url } from "../lib/url";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A friendly, free field guide to stress, sensation, and your own pace. Small invitations, useful ideas, and people worth learning from."
    />
    <title>A little more room · Nervous System Healing</title>
    <link rel="canonical" href={new URL(url(""), Astro.site)} />
    <link rel="icon" href={url("favicon.svg")} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="Nervous System Healing" href={url("rss.xml")} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="site-header wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="#main" aria-label="Nervous System Healing home"
        ><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span
        ><span>nervous system<br />healing</span></a
      >
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#small">Start small</a><a href="#understand">Understand</a
        ><a href="#people">People & paths</a><a href="#research">Sources</a>
      </nav>
      <button class="quiet-button" id="quiet" aria-pressed="false" hidden>
        <span aria-hidden="true">◐</span> Quiet view
      </button>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">
            <span class="tiny-sun" aria-hidden="true">✳</span> A field guide, at
            your pace
          </p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">A little more<br /><em>room</em> to be you.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">
            For the too-much days. The far-away days.<br
              class="desktop-break"
            />
            And the “where do I even begin?” days.
          </p>
          <p class="hero-note">
            Meet your nervous system with curiosity.<br />Find a small place to
            start. Stay as long as you like.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button primary" href="#small"
              >Find a small beginning <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a
            ><a class="text-link" href="#understand"
              >I’d rather just read <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
            >
          </div>
          <p class="small-print">
            Free to explore. No account. Nothing to keep up with.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="hero-art decoration">
          <RoomIllustration />
          <figcaption>
            A place to land. No special breathing required.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>
      <div class="permission-strip">
        <span>You don’t have to feel calm to belong here.</span
        ><span aria-hidden="true">✳</span
        ><span>Curiosity counts. So does stopping.</span>
      </div>

      <HomeChoices />

      <section id="understand" class="understand-band">
        <div class="section wrap">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">02 / A little context</p>
              <h2>Less fixing.<br /><em>More getting to know yourself.</em></h2>
            </div>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href={url("start/1-you-have-a-nervous-system/")}
              >Take the beginner tour ↗</a
            >
          </div>
          <div class="ideas">
            <article>
              <span class="idea-number">01</span>
              <h3>Calm isn’t a character grade.</h3>
              <p>
                You don’t need to turn every feeling into a project. There’s
                room here for energy, uncertainty, rest, and a perfectly
                ordinary Tuesday.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="idea-number">02</span>
              <h3>You get to have preferences.</h3>
              <p>
                Eyes open or closed. Moving or still. Body-focused or
                outward-looking. If an invitation doesn’t fit, changing it is
                allowed.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="idea-number">03</span>
              <h3>A map is still a map.</h3>
              <p>
                Terms like “fight,” “flight,” and “freeze” can start a
                conversation. A website can’t tell what your nervous system is
                doing from a couple of sliders.
              </p>
              <a href="#research">How we handle claims →</a>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="founder wrap section" aria-labelledby="founder-title">
        <div class="founder-art decoration" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>time<br /><em>out.</em></span
          ><svg viewBox="0 0 180 100">
            <path
              d="M18 57Q58 13 90 58t73-3"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2"
            />
            <path
              d="m151 53 13 1-6 13"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2"
            />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The person behind this</p>
          <h2 id="founder-title">
            A place to begin.<br />And to begin <em>again.</em>
          </h2>
          <p>
            This project grows out of Chris’s exploration of burnout, feeling,
            and finding his way back to himself. It gathers questions, useful
            ideas, and ways in for people beginning an exploration of their own.
          </p>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://xnet.fyi/blog/timeout/"
            >Read Chris’s story: Timeout ↗</a
          >
          <p class="small-print">
            Based on the public essay. One person’s experience; not a treatment
            recommendation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <HomePeople />

      <section
        id="research"
        class="section wrap research-section"
        aria-labelledby="research-title"
      >
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">04 / Keep the curiosity. Check the claims.</p>
          <h2 id="research-title">
            A little wonder.<br /><em>A little “how do we know?”</em>
          </h2>
          <p>
            There’s promising work here. There are also open questions. We can
            make room for both.
          </p>
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://www.ptsd.va.gov/professional/treat/txessentials/overview_therapy.asp"
            >Start with established PTSD care guidance ↗</a
          >
        </div>
        <div class="research-notes">
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span
                ><span class="evidence-label">Early research · 2026</span>Can a
                brief somatic session help?</span
              >
            </summary>
            <p>
              Two randomized studies reported encouraging immediate findings.
              They do not establish lasting trauma recovery.
            </p>
            <a
              href="https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/20008066.2026.2613544"
              >Read the study and its limits ↗</a
            >
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span
                ><span class="evidence-label">Active comparison · 2026</span
                >What’s new in parts work?</span
              >
            </summary>
            <p>
              A small trial found improvement in both groups, with no
              significant PTSD symptom advantage for the IFS-based program over
              its active comparison.
            </p>
            <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41609644/"
              >Read the randomized trial abstract ↗</a
            >
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>
              <span
                ><span class="evidence-label">Teaching framework · debated</span
                >Is the nervous system a three-state switch?</span
              >
            </summary>
            <p>
              Polyvagal language is influential, but key physiological claims
              remain contested. We use everyday descriptions without assigning
              you a vagal state.
            </p>
            <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41768017/"
              >Read the critique ↗</a
            ><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41768026/"
              >Read the response ↗</a
            >
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="closing wrap">
        <span class="decoration" aria-hidden="true">✳</span>
        <h2>You can leave<br /><em>some room for later.</em></h2>
        <p>This page will still be here.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="#main">Back to the beginning ↑</a>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap">
      <div>
        <a class="wordmark" href="#main"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>nervous system<br />healing</span></a>
        <p>A free, open-source community resource by <a href="https://crs.land/">Christopher Smothers</a>.<br />Made with curiosity. Contributions welcome.</p>
        <nav class="community-links" aria-label="Open source community">
          <a href="https://github.com/crs48/nervous-system-healing">View the source on GitHub ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/crs48/nervous-system-healing/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contribute ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/crs48/nervous-system-healing/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT license ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="footer-title">A few ways onward</h2>
        <nav class="community-links" aria-label="Explore the guide">
          <a href={url("practices/")}>All practices</a>
          <a href={url("modalities/")}>Approaches to support</a>
          <a href={url("learn/")}>More to understand</a>
          <a href={url("about/why/")}>About this project</a>
          <a href={url("about/criteria/")}>Curation criteria</a>
          <a href={url("rss.xml")}>RSS</a>
        </nav>
        <p>Educational content, not medical advice or a substitute for professional care.
          <a href={url("about/disclaimer/")}>Read the scope and crisis resources</a>.</p>
        <p>Research checked October 10, 2026. No accounts, tracking, sound, or saved selections.</p>
      </div>
    </footer>
    <script>
      import "../scripts/home";
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
